<div class="page">
  <h2>You Should Also Know</h2>
  <div class="section-header">Estimated Tax Penalty</div>
  <p>You may need to increase the federal income tax withheld from your pay, pension, annuity, etc., or make estimated tax payments to avoid an estimated tax penalty based on your household employment taxes shown on Schedule H, line <span data-field="schedule_h_line_22">{{ schedule_h_line_22 }}</span>. You may increase the amount withheld by giving your employer a new Form W-4, or by giving the payer of your pension a new Form W-4P. Make estimated tax payments by filing Form <span data-field="form_number">{{ form_number }}</span>. For more information, see Pub. <span data-field="pub_number">{{ pub_number }}</span>.</p>

  <div class="section-header">What Is the Earned Income Credit (EIC)?</div>
  <p>The EIC is a refundable tax credit for certain workers.</p>
  <p>Which employees must I notify about the EIC? You must notify your household employee about the EIC if you give agreement to withhold federal income tax from the employee's wages but did so because the income tax withholding was required. </p>
  <p>You're encouraged to notify each employee whose wages for 2025 were less than <span data-field="eic_threshold_amount">{{ eic_threshold_amount }}</span> ($88,675 if married filing jointly) that the employee may be eligible for the EIC for 2025.</p>

  <div class="section-header">How and when must I notify my employees?</div>
  <p>You must give the employee one of the following:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The official IRS Form W-2, which has the required information about the EIC on the back of Copy B.</li>
    <li>A substitute Form W-2 with the same EIC information on the back of the employee's copy that is on Copy B of IRS Form W-2.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Notice 797, Possible Federal Tax Refund Due to the Earned Income Credit (EIC).</p>
  <p>Your written statement the same wording as Notice 797.</p>

  <div class="section-header">If the notification isn't given on Form W-2 in a timely manner, you must hand the notice directly to the employee or send it by First-Class Mail to the employee's last known address.</div>

  <div class="section-header">If you're not required to give the employee a Form W-2, you must provide the notification by February <span data-field="date_month">{{ date_month }}</span>, <span data-field="date_year">{{ date_year }}</span>.</div>

  <div class="section-header">How do my employees claim the EIC?</div>
  <p>Eligible employees claim the EIC on their 2025 tax returns.</p>

  <div class="section-header">Rules for Business Employers</div>
  <p>Don't use Schedule H if you chose to report employment taxes for your household employees along with your other employees on Form <span data-field="form_number">{{ form_number }}</span> or <span data-field="form_number_2">{{ form_number_2 }}</span> (sp), Employer's</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2>TREASURY/IRS AND OMB USE ONLY DRAFT</h2>
  <div class="section-header">Quarterly Federal Tax Return; Form 941, Employer's Annual Federal Tax Return for Agricultural Employees; or Form 944, Employer's Annual Federal Tax Return.</div>
  <p>If you are required to withhold federal income tax from your employees' wages on your Form <span data-field="form_number">{{ form_number }}</span>, Employer's Annual Federal Unemployment (FUTA) Tax Return.</p>

  <div class="section-header">State Disability Payments</div>
  <p>Employees are treated as wages subject to social security and Medicare taxes. If your employee received payments from a plan that withheld the employee's share of social security and Medicare taxes, include the payments on Schedule H, line <span data-field="schedule_h_line_22">{{ schedule_h_line_22 }}</span>. If you complete the rest of Part I through line <span data-field="line_number_7">{{ line_number_7 }}</span>, and line <span data-field="line_number_2">{{ line_number_2 }}</span>, and line <span data-field="line_number_6">{{ line_number_6 }}</span>, from that total. Enter the result on these taxes withheld by the state. Enter the result on Schedule H, line <span data-field="schedule_h_line_22">{{ schedule_h_line_22 }}</span>. See the notice issued by the state for more details.</p>

  <div class="section-header">How to Correct Schedule H</div>
  <p>If you discover an error on a Schedule H that you previously filed with Form <span data-field="form_number">{{ form_number }}</span>, <span data-field="form_number_2">{{ form_number_2 }}</span>, or <span data-field="form_number_3">{{ form_number_3 }}</span>, file Form <span data-field="form_number_4">{{ form_number_4 }}</span>, Amended U.S. Individual Income Tax Return, and attach a corrected Schedule H. If you discover an error on a Schedule H that you previously filed with Form <span data-field="form_number">{{ form_number }}</span>, file Form <span data-field="form_number_4">{{ form_number_4 }}</span>, Amended Form <span data-field="form_number_5">{{ form_number_5 }}</span> and attach a corrected Schedule H.</p>

  <div class="section-header">Note. Household employees located in Puerto Rico that were paid from Form <span data-field="form_number">{{ form_number }}</span>, a "Corrected" Form <span data-field="form_number_6">{{ form_number_6 }}</span> and attach a corrected Schedule H.</div>

  <div class="section-header">If you owe tax, pay the tax in full with your Form <span data-field="form_number">{{ form_number }}</span>, "Corrected" Form <span data-field="form_number_7">{{ form_number_7 }}</span>, "Amended" Form <span data-field="form_number_8">{{ form_number_8 }}</span>, or "Amended" Schedule H. If you overpaid tax on a previously filed return, you may claim a refund by filing Form <span data-field="form_number_9">{{ form_number_9 }}</span>.</div>

  <div class="section-header">How to Get Forms and Publications</div>
  <p>To get the IRS forms and publications mentioned in these instructions (including Notice <span data-field="notice_number">{{ notice_number }}</span>), go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov/forms">IRS.gov/Forms</a>.</p>

  <div class="section-header">Privacy Act and Paperwork Reduction Act Notice.</div>
  <p>Ask for the information on this form to carry out the internal Revenue Laws of the United States. You're required to give us the information we need to ensure that you're complying with these laws and to allow us to figure out the correct amount of tax. If you don't provide the information we ask for, we may not be able to process your return.</p>
  <p>You're not required to provide the information requested on a form that is subject to the Paperwork Reduction Act unless the form displays a valid OMB control number.</p>
  <p>Information provided on this form will be retained as long as their contents may become material in the administration of any Internal Revenue Law.</p>

  <div class="section-header">Employee Taxes.</div>
  <p>Taxes of the Internal Revenue Code imposes employment taxes on wages and provides for income tax withholding. This form is used to determine the amount of the taxes that you owe. Section <span data-field="section_number">{{ section_number }}</span> requires you to provide the requested information if the tax is applicable to you. Section <span data-field="section_number_2">{{ section_number_2 }}</span> requires you to provide the information shown on your tax return.</p>
  <p>Generally, tax returns and return information are confidential, as required by section <span data-field="section_number_3">{{ section_number_3 }}</span>. However, section <span data-field="section_number_4">{{ section_number_4 }}</span> allows the IRS to disclose or give the information shown on your tax return to others as described in the Code. For example, we may disclose your tax information to the Department of Justice for civil and criminal litigation, and to cities, states, the District of Columbia, and U.S. commonwealths to administer their tax laws. We may also disclose this</p>

